feat(roster): team admin roster editor + role/tier-gated roster API

Phase 2 of the roster build (Arnel: "Federations should be able to
update. Coaches and admins should be able to manage and accept payments.
Players should be able to manage their own passport.").

The roster API is the write path behind everything the public roster
shows. A bug there silently corrupts a club's roster, and the public
page has no way to report it — it renders whatever is in the database.

AUTHORIZATION — one rule, shared by the page and the API, in
src/lib/team-authority.ts so the UI can never offer an action the server
would refuse. Authority is ROLE-SCOPED PER TEAM, not per user (a person
may coach team A and be a parent rep on team B), and roster rights are
additionally TIER-GATED on the organization track:

  org_free + no role     -> cannot view          (no-claim)
  org_plus + head_coach  -> can view and manage
  org_free + head_coach  -> can view, not manage  (org-plan-required)

The org tier is read through the existing getUserOrgTier(), so the roster
gate and every other org-tier gate cannot disagree. (organizations has no
tier column — the tier lives on profiles.org_tier, with expiry and
cancellation handled by that helper.)

API — /api/manage/team/[id]/roster with GET (read), POST (add), PATCH
(update), DELETE (remove). Two kinds of roster row, because a club's
roster is both things:
  members — people with a RinkStop account, carrying a team ROLE
            (head_coach, player, parent_rep, ...), jersey, position,
            shoots, DOB, and a guardian link for minors
  players — player records linked for a stint, with jersey, position,
            role and a verification source

Rows added here are coach_verified by definition — the team entered them,
so they are not a self-reported claim. That is what makes the public
roster's COACH VERIFIED marker mean something.

Guards added while building it (each caught a real failure):
  - position is validated against
    hockey_player_team_history_position_check (forward|defense|goalie)
  - role is validated against
    hockey_player_team_history_role_check
    (player|captain|alternate_captain|goalie|other)
  - jersey number is validated against the 0-99 CHECK
  - team_name_snapshot is NOT NULL and is populated from the team row —
    it records the team name at the time of the stint so history stays
    readable if the team is later renamed or deactivated
  - a minor cannot be added without a guardian (parent_user_id)
  - duplicate rows return 409 rather than silently duplicating
  - a row must belong to THIS team before it can be updated or deleted

UI — /dashboard/manage/team/[id]/roster, linked from the team settings
page. Members and players are listed separately, each with an editable
role/jersey/position, and a remove button.

New gate: scripts/_test-roster-api.mjs (pre-push Gate 15). Proves against
the live DB that the authorization gate discriminates as above, that the
write path round-trips, and that the database CHECK constraints reject
invalid roles and positions. Everything it creates is rolled back.
